      "commit": {
        "id": "014810e45037ee446612fa752481c7eddf579fd8",
        "message": "fix(operator): send the service hostname as Host on HTTP health probes (w4/m190)\n\nKubelet sent the pod IP as Host, so an app that allowlists its own\nhostnames answered its health path 421 and an HTTP-health deploy could\nnever become Live. HTTP probes now keep connecting to the pod (HTTPGet.Host\nempty) but carry Render's Host header: first verified custom domain\n(spec.host, then spec.hosts; redirect sources skipped), else the canonical\nplatform hostname. Private/worker/TCP probes are unchanged.\n\nThe Host is chosen once per release and retained from the live template\nwhile it carries the same release label, so domain-only edits (operational,\nno deploy row) and the operator upgrade itself do not roll pods. New\nreleases, Restart and rollback select from current domains; cancel and\nfailed-rollout restoration keep the served template verbatim. ADR004 and\nthe ADR018 parity row record the rule and the unverified Render timing."
      },
